# Files an agent is not supposed to edit on its own authority.
#
# A write lock stated in a prompt is a suggestion. Requiring a human review on these paths is
# what makes it cost something to cross the boundary. Replace @your-org/... with real teams
# and enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection, or this file does nothing.

# Tests are owned by the test designer. A pull request that changes an assertion to make the
# build pass must be looked at by a person.
/src/test/                      @your-org/engineering

# Business rules. An invented threshold that lands here becomes production behaviour.
/docs/specs/                    @your-org/product

# The gates themselves. Weakening a rule must never be quieter than following it.
/config/checkstyle/             @your-org/engineering
/src/test/resources/archunit.properties  @your-org/engineering
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/engineering
/.github/agents/                @your-org/engineering
/scripts/check-write-lock.sh    @your-org/engineering
